# Currency display

Do not format money with `toLocaleString`, string concat, or ad-hoc rounding. Use helpers from `@shared/utils/helpers/general`. Call them in the template; do not wrap a single call in an extra `computed`.

## Fiat — `formatDollars`

```vue
{{ formatDollars(row.amount_usd) }}
{{ formatDollars(item.amount, "$", "—", 2) }}
```

Signature: `formatDollars(amount, currencyValue = "$", errorValue = "—", countPartMoreOneDollar = 0, countPartLessOneDollar = 2, isFormattedIntegerPart = true)`.

Pass `""` as `currencyValue` when the symbol should be omitted.

## Crypto — `formatAmountBlockchain`

```vue
{{ formatAmountBlockchain(item.amount, item.currency_id) }} {{ getCurrentCoin(item.currency_id) }}
```

Always pass `currencyId` (`USDT.Tron`, `BTC.Bitcoin`) so precision comes from `DEFAULT_CURRENCIES_INFO`.

## Currency id — `COIN.Blockchain`

- Ticker: `getCurrentCoin("USDT.Tron")` → `USDT`
- Network: `getCurrentBlockchain("USDT.Tron")` → `Tron`

Do not `split(".")` inline.
